1
00:00:05,363 --> 00:00:13,693
Record a diagnosis — Clinical ▸ Diagnoses — Code a problem properly, so the claim behind it is accepted first time.

2
00:00:19,107 --> 00:00:28,510
Diagnoses now sits under Clinical, not Patients — it is coding work, so it lives beside the other clinical modules.

3
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:37,589
This is the practice-wide problem list, filtered by patient or by status.

4
00:00:37,590 --> 00:00:44,164
The form opens above the list and pushes it down, so nothing you were reading is hidden behind it.

5
00:00:44,164 --> 00:00:59,120
Opened from here there is no patient in context, so the form asks for one — with the MRN alongside, to separate namesakes.

6
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:08,107
The plain-English name is what your colleagues read. It is not what pays.

7
00:01:08,107 --> 00:01:17,655
ICD-10 codes are searched, not remembered — type the code or the words and take it from the list.

8
00:01:17,655 --> 00:01:27,384
Picked from the database, the code is current and it exists.

9
00:01:27,384 --> 00:01:39,020
Active, resolved or chronic is the line the next clinician reads first — and the one that goes stale if nobody updates it.

10
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:56,657
The note travels with the diagnosis, so the reasoning is attached to the code.

11
00:01:56,657 --> 00:02:01,372
Saved to the problem list, and to that patient’s chart.

12
00:02:01,372 --> 00:02:09,439
From here the code carries: onto the claim, where the payer checks it against the procedure, and into the patient’s portal.

13
00:02:11,304 --> 00:02:26,744
What you just did

14
00:02:28,894 --> 00:02:37,894
Health | Efficiency | Growth — More in the Getting Started series — the next video is linked on screen.
